# New C# types — name before you code

Before adding or **renaming** a public type under `Assets/Scripts/` or `Assets/Tests/`:

1. Read **`.cursor/review-config.json`** → **`classNaming.patternsDoc`** (decision flow + locked suffix rules).
2. Follow **class-naming-grid-dungeon** skill when choosing suffix, assembly, or folder.
3. Skim **`classNaming.suffixRule`** ([unity-csharp-class-suffix-patterns](unity-csharp-class-suffix-patterns.mdc)) for the assembly → suffix table.
4. Use **`classNaming.shippedTypesDoc`** only to avoid duplicate type names — not to invent suffixes.

Review enforcement: [code-review-config](code-review-config.mdc) + **fresh-reviewer** when the diff adds or renames types.
